ore Tamisier's invention, the orientation of a cylindro-conical bullet tended to remain along its inertial axis, progressively setting it against its trajectory and increasingly meeting air resistance, which rendered the bullet's movement erratic.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEratic_bullet_trajectory.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Minie_Balls.jpg/500px-Minie_Balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Minie_Balls.jpg/500px-Minie_Balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Minié ball ammunition","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMinie_Balls.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Minie_ball_design_harpers_ferry_burton.jpg/500px-Minie_ball_design_harpers_ferry_burton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Minie_ball_design_harpers_ferry_burton.jpg/500px-Minie_ball_design_harpers_ferry_burton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1855 Minié ball design from the U.S. Arsenal, Harper's Ferry, West Virginia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMinie_ball_design_harpers_ferry_burton.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Bullet_types_on_.270_ammunition.jpg/500px-Bullet_types_on_.270_ammunition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Bullet_types_on_.270_ammunition.jpg/500px-Bullet_types_on_.270_ammunition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":".270 Winchester ammunition:100-grain (6.5 g) – hollow point115-grain (7.5 g) – FMJBT130-grain (8.4 g) – soft point150-grain (9.7 g) – round nose","link":"